                            <comment id="16354920" author="zjffdu" created="Wed, 7 Feb 2018 03:50:12 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;It seems python specific issue, it works correctly for spark interpreter&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16354986" author="mebelousov" created="Wed, 7 Feb 2018 05:35:51 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I have been testing more. The restart of spark or JDBC interpreters in note also aborts running interpreter in other notes.&lt;br/&gt;
Thank you for including this issue to blockers of 0.8.0.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16355045" author="githubbot" created="Wed, 7 Feb 2018 06:52:44 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;GitHub user zjffdu opened a pull request:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/2769&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/2769&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-3171&quot; title=&quot;Restart of interpreter in note also aborts running interpreter in another note&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-3171&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-3171&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. Restart of interpreter in note also aborts running interpreter in another note&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;
		&lt;ol&gt;
			&lt;li&gt;What is this PR for?&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;/ol&gt;
		&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;    The root cause is that in isolated mode interpreters will share the same scheduler. That means when one interpreter is terminated, all the running jobs under the scheduler of this interpreter will be aborted too. This PR will create one scheduler for each session. So when one session is closed, only the running jobs under this session&apos;s scheduler is aborted. &lt;/p&gt;

